WEBVTT

00:00:00.679 --> 00:00:05.601
<i>When I heard Kurose</i>
<i>had offered him this mission,</i>

00:00:06.018 --> 00:00:08.270
<i>I thought this might happen.</i>

00:00:09.146 --> 00:00:10.940
<i>But I didn't stop him.</i>

00:00:12.066 --> 00:00:16.403
<i>I knew that this was very important.</i>

00:00:18.405 --> 00:00:20.783
That's why I'm taking part, too.

00:00:24.745 --> 00:00:27.581
This is the path he chose.

00:00:28.249 --> 00:00:29.458
It's not your fault.

00:00:38.259 --> 00:00:41.095
Thank you for mourning him.

00:00:42.137 --> 00:00:43.430
Thank you.

00:02:16.273 --> 00:02:21.111
Is it really possible to use Cell
Assembler Two to treat wounds?

00:02:21.654 --> 00:02:26.825
I thought the only case of their use
in a live body was on Dr. Kiryu.

00:02:26.950 --> 00:02:31.538
No wonder Kanzaki is able to
survive outside without a mask.

00:02:32.039 --> 00:02:34.500
It's a good excuse
for testing on humans,

00:02:34.583 --> 00:02:36.668
since he's a pre-Burst victim.

00:02:36.752 --> 00:02:39.922
Even so, what he said still pissed me off!

00:02:41.215 --> 00:02:43.842
Accepting a life-threatening mission means

00:02:44.051 --> 00:02:47.137
that you're prepared to die
from the very start.

00:02:47.805 --> 00:02:49.807
Or maybe in your heart,

00:02:49.932 --> 00:02:54.228
you weren't taking the threat
to your life seriously.

00:02:55.354 --> 00:02:57.815
Is he trying to get rid of us?

00:02:58.399 --> 00:02:59.608
Then, I swear I'll--

00:02:59.691 --> 00:03:00.526
That's right.

00:03:01.443 --> 00:03:05.531
He knew if he said that, we'd be
too proud not to finish the mission.

00:03:06.532 --> 00:03:08.283
He knows us too well.

00:03:08.367 --> 00:03:11.537
Damn, that's one clever kid.

00:03:13.497 --> 00:03:16.375
<i>-Do you trust him?</i>
<i>-What?</i>

00:03:16.959 --> 00:03:19.711
How much have you heard
about this mission?

00:03:20.295 --> 00:03:21.713
Well...

00:03:29.304 --> 00:03:30.973
Why didn't you tell me

00:03:31.765 --> 00:03:34.309
that when we get the real me,

00:03:34.476 --> 00:03:37.354
the other me will disappear?

00:03:38.772 --> 00:03:39.940
Shiraishi told you?

00:03:40.816 --> 00:03:41.900
Is it true?

00:03:43.110 --> 00:03:45.738
I'm returning you to the way
you should be.

00:03:46.238 --> 00:03:47.656
The human to the human,

00:03:47.740 --> 00:03:49.408
the artificial to the artificial.

00:03:51.034 --> 00:03:52.161
Artificial...

00:03:52.745 --> 00:03:54.538
Besides, that artificial part

00:03:54.705 --> 00:03:57.332
is the cause of the Burst.

00:03:57.916 --> 00:04:01.545
Unless the cause is removed,
the Burst can't be ended.

00:04:02.129 --> 00:04:07.593
But this body I have right now
is the duplicate, right?

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:12.306
And the girl that I contact in my dreams
is the duplicate brain, right?

00:04:12.890 --> 00:04:14.641
But destroying her...

00:04:15.267 --> 00:04:16.477
means killing her!

00:04:17.269 --> 00:04:19.062
In simple terms, yes.

00:04:19.855 --> 00:04:23.609
You'll be separated.
The process will reverse your creation.

00:04:23.942 --> 00:04:27.362
The other you isn't human.
There's no need to sympathize with her.

00:04:30.532 --> 00:04:34.286
This must be something
that I just can't understand.

00:04:35.204 --> 00:04:39.249
You're doing something
that only you can understand, Kanzaki.

00:04:47.549 --> 00:04:50.427
It's okay for me to trust you, right?

00:04:59.561 --> 00:05:00.521
Human forms!

00:05:03.649 --> 00:05:04.858
Aiko!

00:05:09.112 --> 00:05:13.283
All right, whatever happens,
we'll get you to Primary Point.

00:05:13.367 --> 00:05:16.662
But once this mission is over,
we're strangers again.

00:05:16.745 --> 00:05:18.080
That's my intention.

00:05:18.163 --> 00:05:20.374
-Let's go, Aiko!
-Hey!

00:05:22.584 --> 00:05:23.919
Tachibana, does it hurt?

00:05:24.002 --> 00:05:25.754
<i>I didn't sense it! Why?</i>

00:05:26.922 --> 00:05:28.090
<i>This is strange.</i>

00:05:28.423 --> 00:05:30.467
<i>Is there another root Matter?</i>

00:05:33.387 --> 00:05:34.972
<i>Activity in Area Five and Six!</i>

00:05:35.556 --> 00:05:38.559
At this rate,
it'll overflow the dams again!

00:05:48.819 --> 00:05:52.656
<i>Tomorrow will be the seventh day</i>
<i>since we entered the Area.</i>

00:05:52.990 --> 00:05:56.034
<i>We have to reach Primary Point tomorrow,</i>

00:05:56.368 --> 00:05:59.162
<i>before the other you loses consciousness.</i>

00:05:59.663 --> 00:06:03.417
I wonder what it will feel like
when I disappear.

00:06:04.585 --> 00:06:06.837
There's no feeling when you disappear.

00:06:07.462 --> 00:06:11.008
It's just like falling asleep.

00:06:11.633 --> 00:06:14.428
You won't know that
you've lost consciousness.

00:06:14.511 --> 00:06:16.013
The rest is tranquil sleep.

00:06:17.097 --> 00:06:19.141
You talk as if you know about it.

00:06:23.353 --> 00:06:24.354
In other words,

00:06:24.438 --> 00:06:27.816
Isazu knew the Matter's activity
and Yuzuha's are linked.

00:06:28.525 --> 00:06:32.029
I always thought you two
shared everything.

00:06:32.613 --> 00:06:35.365
I thought so, too. Until now.

00:06:41.830 --> 00:06:45.667
I can see the final gate, K5!

00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:52.090
Beyond that wall is Kiryu
Biotech Research Facility Two.

00:06:52.299 --> 00:06:54.051
Primary Point!

00:06:54.676 --> 00:06:57.512
Okay, let's climb that giant dam!

00:06:57.679 --> 00:06:59.389
See you there, if we survive!

00:06:59.473 --> 00:07:00.515
-Wilco!
-Wilco!

00:07:02.684 --> 00:07:07.439
<i>Shiraishi and our two clients will take</i>
<i>the left ramp to the top of the dam.</i>

00:07:07.940 --> 00:07:11.193
<i>Seri and Misawa will go up the wall</i>
<i>from the right.</i>

00:07:18.909 --> 00:07:23.455
<i>Kazuki and I will distract the Matter</i>
<i>as we climb up the front of the dam.</i>

00:07:50.190 --> 00:07:51.024
It's coming!

00:08:44.870 --> 00:08:46.329
It saved us?

00:08:46.538 --> 00:08:47.497
The Matter?

00:08:47.581 --> 00:08:49.583
-Hurry!
-Let's go!

00:08:50.709 --> 00:08:52.335
<i>This dam has no Guillotine.</i>

00:08:52.419 --> 00:08:54.212
The shock's effect is limited.

00:08:55.088 --> 00:08:56.089
Prepare yourself.

00:08:56.381 --> 00:08:57.632
Get ready, Tachibana.

00:08:57.716 --> 00:08:58.550
Okay.

00:09:01.219 --> 00:09:02.220
-Now!
-Now!

00:09:27.829 --> 00:09:30.707
<i>This is the last place I visited</i>
<i>with my father.</i>

00:09:32.167 --> 00:09:34.586
<i>This is where Mom and Ryota are.</i>

00:09:35.337 --> 00:09:37.631
<i>It's where the disaster began.</i>

00:09:38.048 --> 00:09:39.633
<i>Primary Point.</i>

00:09:43.512 --> 00:09:45.514
<i>What? It's already moving?</i>

00:09:45.597 --> 00:09:46.515
<i>Go!</i>

00:09:47.265 --> 00:09:50.018
<i>The entrance is clogged with Matter.</i>

00:09:51.728 --> 00:09:55.107
<i>We'll enter through</i>
<i>the water intake and climb the shaft.</i>

00:09:55.190 --> 00:09:58.401
<i>From there, we'll head to the bottom</i>
<i>of the facility,</i>

00:09:58.485 --> 00:10:02.572
<i>and head for our final destination,</i>
<i>the surgical system, ALSUS.</i>

00:10:15.418 --> 00:10:17.838
<i>Things are looking bad,</i>
<i>Director Nanbara.</i>

00:10:17.921 --> 00:10:20.674
The opposition party is permitting
limited use of weapons

00:10:20.799 --> 00:10:24.344
by the Self-Defense Forces
within Ground Zero.

00:10:35.230 --> 00:10:36.815
Okay, we're finally here.

00:10:39.860 --> 00:10:40.694
Tachibana!

00:10:45.782 --> 00:10:46.825
That's the place!

00:10:51.663 --> 00:10:52.622
Dad...

00:10:53.290 --> 00:10:58.086
I swear that I'll save Mom and Ryota.

00:11:00.964 --> 00:11:04.759
The root of all the Matter.
The origin of the Burst.

00:11:04.926 --> 00:11:07.178
Our target is the bottom level.

00:11:09.723 --> 00:11:10.807
Okay, let's go!

00:11:10.891 --> 00:11:11.808
<i>Aiko!</i>

00:11:12.976 --> 00:11:15.562
<i>You know not to leave</i>
<i>the hospital like that.</i>

00:11:16.271 --> 00:11:17.314
Who's that?

00:11:17.856 --> 00:11:19.691
Dr. Isazu?

00:11:20.275 --> 00:11:21.651
<i>Come back.</i>

00:11:21.943 --> 00:11:24.613
<i>I won't do anything to make you unhappy,</i>

00:11:25.030 --> 00:11:27.741
<i>unlike that transfer student.</i>

00:11:30.410 --> 00:11:31.494
Kanzaki?

00:11:32.287 --> 00:11:34.497
I know him well.

00:11:34.789 --> 00:11:37.500
And I know why he has taken you there.

00:11:39.085 --> 00:11:42.547
I never thought we would be able to
talk like this again.

00:11:42.881 --> 00:11:44.257
It's been a long time,

00:11:44.341 --> 00:11:46.509
<i>Toshihide Yura.</i>

00:11:48.970 --> 00:11:50.055
What?

00:11:51.348 --> 00:11:54.643
Toshihide Yura... That can't be!

00:11:55.268 --> 00:11:56.436
Who's that?

00:11:56.519 --> 00:11:57.938
You don't know?

00:11:58.021 --> 00:12:01.483
He's the genius who invented
that Live Suit you've got on!

00:12:01.566 --> 00:12:03.401
Seriously? This guy?

00:12:03.485 --> 00:12:07.572
No way. He died in the Burst.

00:12:07.739 --> 00:12:10.283
Dr. Isazu, what are you saying?

00:12:10.367 --> 00:12:13.119
<i>He survived.</i>

00:12:15.372 --> 00:12:19.751
By transplanting his own brain
into the duplicate body

00:12:19.876 --> 00:12:22.212
of a boy he never knew, Yuya Kanzaki.

00:12:22.796 --> 00:12:26.341
The serial number
of the sacrificed duplicate body is

00:12:26.967 --> 00:12:30.095
20210001.

00:12:32.347 --> 00:12:33.264
Excuse me.

00:12:36.351 --> 00:12:38.019
NAME: YUYA KANZAKI

00:12:38.103 --> 00:12:42.649
Artificial organism
serial number 20210001.

00:12:44.734 --> 00:12:48.446
This is Artificial Organism
duplicate body Unit One.

00:12:49.739 --> 00:12:51.032
Isazu,

00:12:51.199 --> 00:12:54.244
what's the point in revealing that secret?

00:12:54.828 --> 00:12:55.996
This can't be real.

00:12:56.079 --> 00:12:57.872
No wonder he knows everything.

00:13:00.458 --> 00:13:01.835
Damn!

00:13:01.918 --> 00:13:04.671
You mean we didn't delete all the data?

00:13:04.796 --> 00:13:06.589
Was it on a standalone server?

00:13:06.673 --> 00:13:10.051
That old Kiryu's security
was way too tight.

00:13:10.343 --> 00:13:11.511
Hey, hold on here!

00:13:11.636 --> 00:13:13.763
You knew Toshihide Yura was alive?

00:13:14.347 --> 00:13:17.183
I didn't just know.
I performed the transplant.

00:13:17.726 --> 00:13:19.102
Why didn't you tell me?

00:13:19.686 --> 00:13:22.856
If I did, you never would have
let him enter the Area

00:13:22.939 --> 00:13:24.357
on such a dangerous mission.

00:13:26.860 --> 00:13:28.903
<i>Did you all know</i>

00:13:29.154 --> 00:13:34.200
<i>that the surgery that man there</i>
<i>performed on Aiko Tachibana</i>

00:13:34.325 --> 00:13:36.202
<i>was the cause of the Burst.</i>

00:13:37.370 --> 00:13:39.205
Aiko's surgery?

00:13:39.372 --> 00:13:41.541
You caused the Burst?

00:13:42.042 --> 00:13:46.463
I bet there's one more thing
you didn't know, Aiko.

00:13:46.796 --> 00:13:48.840
To end the Burst,

00:13:49.424 --> 00:13:55.513
<i>your brain and your body</i>
<i>must be destroyed.</i>

00:13:59.225 --> 00:14:00.769
But...

00:14:01.478 --> 00:14:03.646
The fake one will be destroyed!

00:14:03.855 --> 00:14:05.482
<i>That's right.</i>

00:14:11.988 --> 00:14:15.033
The fake one is me?

00:14:18.745 --> 00:14:19.954
Is that right?

00:14:20.747 --> 00:14:21.623
Kanzaki!

00:14:27.420 --> 00:14:29.339
<i>What's this?</i>

00:14:30.173 --> 00:14:31.966
<i>Where is this?</i>

00:14:40.100 --> 00:14:42.560
<i>That's me. I'm injured.</i>

00:14:43.269 --> 00:14:46.022
<i>Oh, right. I was in a car accident.</i>

00:14:47.899 --> 00:14:50.443
<i>And Dr. Yura performed the surgery.</i>

00:14:51.152 --> 00:14:56.449
<i>What? Then why do I see myself?</i>

00:14:57.075 --> 00:14:59.452
<i>How is it I'm able to see myself?</i>

00:15:18.847 --> 00:15:20.056
Is it true?

00:15:21.099 --> 00:15:23.476
Aiko Tachibana's duplicate body panicked

00:15:23.560 --> 00:15:28.314
when its brain was removed,
and underwent abnormal cell proliferation,

00:15:28.648 --> 00:15:30.900
creating the Malignant Matter.

00:15:31.818 --> 00:15:33.611
That was the Burst.

00:15:33.695 --> 00:15:37.282
In other words, your body is the Matter.

00:15:37.866 --> 00:15:41.161
For you to return to your body

00:15:41.369 --> 00:15:44.873
means that you must become the Matter.

00:15:46.040 --> 00:15:48.376
I'll become the Matter?

00:15:49.169 --> 00:15:54.090
For Yura to end the Burst,
he'll induce apoptosis in your brain.

00:15:54.674 --> 00:15:57.844
In other words, he'll cause your cells
to commit suicide

00:15:57.927 --> 00:16:01.806
by injecting you with a medication
called Anti-Cell Assembler.

00:16:02.640 --> 00:16:06.978
<i>Then, he'll return your brain</i>
<i>to the artificial organism body</i>

00:16:07.312 --> 00:16:10.857
<i>so it annihilates your body</i>
<i>that has turned into the Matter.</i>

00:16:12.108 --> 00:16:14.194
<i>To him, your brain</i>

00:16:14.277 --> 00:16:17.947
<i>is nothing more than a tool</i>
<i>to save the real Aiko Tachibana.</i>

00:16:18.948 --> 00:16:22.660
<i>However, I don't want to lose you.</i>

00:16:22.911 --> 00:16:24.162
<i>That's because</i>

00:16:24.370 --> 00:16:26.873
<i>you are the only artificial organism brain</i>

00:16:26.956 --> 00:16:29.292
<i>that has ever obtained consciousness.</i>

00:16:30.919 --> 00:16:34.005
<i>Soon, the Self-Defense Forces</i>
<i>will attack the Matter</i>

00:16:34.088 --> 00:16:36.007
<i>in the Area to wipe it out.</i>

00:16:36.090 --> 00:16:37.133
-What?
-What?

00:16:37.300 --> 00:16:40.553
<i>If you evacuate to the hazard shelter</i>
<i>in the basement</i>

00:16:40.637 --> 00:16:44.349
<i>on the opposite side of the facility</i>
<i>until the attack is over,</i>

00:16:44.432 --> 00:16:46.267
<i>you'll survive.</i>

00:16:46.643 --> 00:16:49.020
<i>Come back to me...</i>

00:16:55.485 --> 00:16:59.155
I cut the communication,
but it'll be back online before long.

00:17:00.114 --> 00:17:04.035
For Yuzuha's sake, he plans to prevent
Yura from ending the Burst.

00:17:04.619 --> 00:17:05.703
So it seems.

00:17:07.830 --> 00:17:12.544
At any rate, I appreciate that
you saved the life of Toshihide Yura,

00:17:13.002 --> 00:17:15.713
and that you told me
Isazu's true intentions.

00:17:16.256 --> 00:17:17.215
Then...

00:17:17.966 --> 00:17:20.802
can you stop
the Self-Defense Forces' attack?

00:17:22.387 --> 00:17:26.558
Wait! There's a serial number on my eye!

00:17:27.058 --> 00:17:30.728
Isn't that proof that this body
is the fake one?

00:17:30.895 --> 00:17:31.729
Then...

00:17:31.813 --> 00:17:33.606
Wait. I'll have a look.

00:17:36.234 --> 00:17:37.944
I'll share the data.

00:17:39.612 --> 00:17:44.117
There it is. Serial number 20210002.

00:17:44.701 --> 00:17:46.411
It's duplicate body Unit Two.

00:17:47.120 --> 00:17:48.454
Then, I really am...

00:17:49.038 --> 00:17:50.039
Amazing!

00:17:50.164 --> 00:17:52.917
Then, that means... Shiraishi?

00:17:56.087 --> 00:17:57.255
Shiraishi?

00:17:58.631 --> 00:17:59.632
Shiraishi!

00:18:03.511 --> 00:18:06.180
Isn't that so, Shiraishi?

00:18:07.890 --> 00:18:10.602
Aiko, your eyes are part of your brain.

00:18:10.685 --> 00:18:11.728
What?

00:18:12.645 --> 00:18:17.400
Artificial organism eyes
are made as part of the brain.

00:18:19.485 --> 00:18:23.656
That means if there's
an inscription on the eyes...

00:18:24.240 --> 00:18:25.325
Aiko,

00:18:25.700 --> 00:18:29.287
it means that your brain is artificial.

00:18:31.748 --> 00:18:36.002
But it's impossible to introduce
carbon nanostructures into a real body!

00:18:36.669 --> 00:18:38.630
<i>If</i> it were an entirely real body.

00:18:39.547 --> 00:18:45.261
If Cell Assembler Two was used
to repair her injuries during surgery,

00:18:45.386 --> 00:18:47.889
then those parts
are artificial organisms.

00:18:47.972 --> 00:18:49.349
So it <i>would</i> be possible

00:18:49.432 --> 00:18:53.102
for carbon nanostructures
to coexist with the original body.

00:18:53.728 --> 00:18:54.771
Am I wrong?

00:18:56.314 --> 00:18:57.649
You're exactly right.

00:18:58.691 --> 00:19:02.320
Then, when Isazu introduced that,

00:19:02.445 --> 00:19:04.113
it triggered the Burst.

00:19:05.406 --> 00:19:09.202
I bet Isazu himself
doesn't even realize that.

00:19:10.203 --> 00:19:12.330
How can you act like it's nothing?

00:19:13.122 --> 00:19:17.293
But I can think for myself!
I can feel! I have thoughts!

00:19:18.294 --> 00:19:20.797
I remember everything since I was a child!

00:19:21.255 --> 00:19:24.467
So how can I still be a fake?

00:19:25.551 --> 00:19:30.014
I created your mind
in order to save Aiko Tachibana.

00:19:30.723 --> 00:19:34.060
You're AICO, the Aiko Tachibana duplicate.

00:19:36.270 --> 00:19:39.065
<i>Your real body caused the Burst,</i>

00:19:39.273 --> 00:19:42.402
<i>and became the Matter</i>
<i>that has overrun the Area.</i>

00:19:42.860 --> 00:19:45.988
<i>The fault for that lies with me.</i>

00:19:46.406 --> 00:19:48.032
<i>And to take responsibility,</i>

00:19:48.574 --> 00:19:51.577
<i>I will return you to where you belong.</i>

00:19:52.245 --> 00:19:55.456
I have to complete the treatment
of Aiko Tachibana.

00:19:56.040 --> 00:19:57.542
What? But...

00:19:58.793 --> 00:20:02.964
Then let's get going! Merge her
with the Matter and end this Burst.

00:20:04.048 --> 00:20:07.552
Damn! An artificial brain?
That's one crazy zombie.

00:20:07.635 --> 00:20:08.720
Sagami!

00:20:12.849 --> 00:20:16.477
Hey, kid, I think your words
are contradicting your actions.

00:20:16.561 --> 00:20:17.979
What?

00:20:21.858 --> 00:20:22.859
Oh, shit!

00:20:23.693 --> 00:20:25.236
-Haruka, Evidence!
-Wait!

00:20:25.319 --> 00:20:27.238
Aiko, we have to escape!

00:20:28.740 --> 00:20:30.283
-Aiko!
-Tachibana!

00:20:30.366 --> 00:20:31.701
-Stop!
-Oh, no!

00:20:33.453 --> 00:20:34.537
Aiko!

00:20:34.620 --> 00:20:35.621
Tachibana!

00:20:36.330 --> 00:20:40.752
<i>I want you to send a team to Primary Point</i>
<i>to retrieve Aiko Tachibana.</i>

00:20:41.377 --> 00:20:44.130
Sorry, but I can't approve that.

00:20:44.714 --> 00:20:45.923
I'll see to this.

00:20:46.299 --> 00:20:49.135
Can you leave it to my discretion?

00:20:58.102 --> 00:21:02.857
I knew it. The only person
who can save you is me.

00:21:43.731 --> 00:21:44.607
Gummi?

00:21:46.776 --> 00:21:47.610
What?

00:22:03.835 --> 00:22:06.420
<i>Thank you for coming.</i>

00:22:24.105 --> 00:22:25.648
Nice to meet you.

00:22:26.774 --> 00:22:28.276
You're the other me.

00:23:57.782 --> 00:23:59.992
Subtitle translation by Brian Athey
